The system prompt texts in hooks/prompts/ (orchestrator, role prompts, council
mode and its synthesis format) are adapted from oh-my-opencode-slim,
https://github.com/alvinunreal/oh-my-opencode-slim (src/agents/orchestrator.ts,
role-routing.ts, role-prompts.ts, council.ts and src/hooks/council-inject),
licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Changes: rewritten for Claude Code's Agent tool and Pantheon's delegate,
delegate_result and delegate_cancel tools; opencode-only parts (todo
continuity, marketplace, wait_for_user, question, task_message) removed; the
librarian points to web search and the available documentation MCPs; every
role prompt ends with a line that lets a task's report format replace the
role's own.

The plugin was first developed in https://github.com/anderson-spider/claude-workflow-codex
(PR #4), a fork of https://github.com/scasella/claude-dynamic-workflows-codex
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Stephen Casella); none of that project's code remains.

Pantheon panel

The rail and elapsed surface modules, native subagent tracking and tool-input
description/redaction are ported from scasella/claude-flightdeck 0.3.2,
https://github.com/scasella/claude-flightdeck
(commit f31daca523d36c501cd0df23a737a44c7dc56ad6), by Stephen Casella,
licensed under the MIT License reproduced below.

Changes: rails use engine colors and support vertical as well as horizontal
connectors; a pulsing state glyph marks active roles. Live clocks resync with
hook readings. Native subagent tracking uses pure reducers, groups rounds by
turnId and keeps a bounded roster in Pantheon's session state. Tool activity
uses short descriptions with common credential patterns redacted. The panel
joins native agents and Codex jobs in fixed role slots, with Agents and Jobs
tabs and docked, inline mini and desktop layouts. The permission gate, model
loops, turn receipt, session log, architect timeline and configuration were
not ported. Tracking hooks still pass every event on unchanged.

